From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] smb: client: select CPU/DMA CMAC by size and preserve signature failures

Allow asynchronous hardware CMAC providers, including SG2002 CryptoDMA.
Use synchronous providers below the measured 320-byte per-message cutoff,
selecting before key setup so short signatures submit no DMA. Use request-owned
transforms to avoid concurrent verification/signing key races. Extract kernel
pages into a bounded scatterlist rather than passing temporary local mappings
to async callbacks; preserve the original iterators. Keep a software provider
available. Propagate signature errors and withhold unauthenticated compound
response buffers, otherwise a later wire-status mapping can mask the error.
Distinguish bad signatures from server ACL errors.

--- a/fs/smb/client/Kconfig
+++ b/fs/smb/client/Kconfig
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 	select CRYPTO_CCM
 	select CRYPTO_GCM
 	select CRYPTO_AES
-	select CRYPTO_LIB_AES_CBC_MACS
+	select CRYPTO_CMAC
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_ARC4
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_MD5
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_SHA256
